   "TerminalID": "T100000131094",
   "UnitID": "G100002109401",
   "Wiki": "https://www.gem.wiki/Manzanillo_(Dominican_Republic)_LNG_Terminal",
   "TerminalName": "Energía 2000 Manzanillo FSRU",
   "UnitName": "--",
   "FacilityType": "import",
   "FacilityType [ref]": "https://eyr.com.do/manzanillo-primer-cargamento-gas-natural-mpl/",
   "Fuel": "LNG",
   "Status": "operating",
   "Substatus": "actual",
   "Status [ref]": "https://www.diariolibre.com/economia/energia/2026/01/08/energia-2000-recibe-cargamento-de-gas-natural-para-su-central/3398529, https://presidencia.gob.do/noticias/presidente-abinader-inaugura-termoelectrica-manzanillo-power-land-que-incorpora-414-mw-al",
   "Country/Area": "Dominican Republic",
   "Researcher": "Gregor Clark",
   "LastUpdated": "2026-08-06",
   "ResearcherNotesUnit": "Gregor, Aug 2026: Financially troubled NFE abandoned its charter agreement for the Energos Freeze FSRU and returned control to Energos in Nov 2025. First LNG cargo was delivered in January 2026 to supply test operations at the associated Manzanillo Power Land gas plant, and the plant began commercial operations in March 2026. \n\nGC, Oct 2025: FSRU Energos Freeze arrived at Manzanillo in late Aug 2025: https://www.diariolibre.com/economia/energia/2025/08/31/manzanillo-power-land-recibe-buque-que-garantiza-gas-natural/3229742.  However,  as of Sep 2025 vessel operator NFE was said to be close to bankruptcy, potentially complicating the project's development: https://deultimominuto.net/economia/new-fortress-energy/\n\nAL,Jul 2025: Construction is probably nearly complete; Energos Freeze will begin supplying Energia2000's Manzanillo PowerLand plant as soon as September 2025, according to several news sources (power plant is nearly operational https://dr1.com/news/2025/01/29/natural-gas-plant-expected-to-inject-414-mw-into-power-grid-starting-summer/). This might be a temporary arrangement? It's still a bit unclear. In April 2025, TotalEnergies signed an agreement to supply 0.4 million tons of LNG to Enadom to power one of Manzanillo's power plants - to begin 2027. \nGC, Sep 2024: Construction of the project officially began with a July 2024 groundbreaking ceremony hosted by Dominican president Luis Abinader; Gregor, July 2023: Dominican government awarded this project to Manzanillo Gas & Power in June 2022, to be completed within a 42-month time frame. Still no definitive news of construction as of July 2023.",
   "ResearcherNotesProject": "Gregor, Aug 2026:  Note that this project is entirely separate from the Manzanillo Gas & Power LNG Terminal (Project ID: L100001084797) currently under construction in the same Manzanillo port area. GEM has conflated these two projects in the past, but I have now split them into separate database entries.\n\nChanged vessel owner from New Fortress Energy (NFE) to Energos, based on NFE's November 2025 termination of its charter agreement with Energos for the Energos Freeze, and \"novation\" of its associated sub-charter agreements to Energos: https://ir.newfortressenergy.com/static-files/907e3b52-978d-4934-87b9-5023cecf266f\n\nAmalia July 2025: This terminal is part of an integrated energy project in the DR involving the LNG terminal and three gas plants operated by different companies. One plant (Block 01, Manzanillo Gas & Power) appears linked to the LNG terminal development, but the terminal is expected to supply all three. Manzanillo PowerLand is nearly operational and will charter the Energos Freeze FSRU (announced July 2025). Although some sources claim the LNG terminal is owned by Energia 2000 (operator of the combustion plant), our database and supporting documents (e.g. the ESIA for Block 02 - see source sapfnidbinvestrm-183122) indicate the terminal is actually owned/operated by Manzanillo Gas & Power. Based on available info, I’ve marked the terminal as offshore/floating (FSRU), and I've added the Energos Freeze as a vessel. This is still somewhat unclear, since other sources claim it's an onshore terminal: https://ehplus.do/central-gas-natural-manzanillo-power-land-alcanza-usdn-73-de-avance-y-aportara-414-mw-en-2025/. For now, technically, the FSRU that is meant to arrive in September is being charted and not operated by Energia 2000, although the terminal is owned by Manzanillo Gas&Power. As per Rob's suggestion, I'm adding Energia 2000 as an operator, so that this is more apparent in the data. Update in the future when there's more info (didn't add to wiki just yet, until it's more clear).",
